Job Description 
 Build the future with us! 
 As an Enterprise Architect, you will play a key role in the organization’s transformation and modernization by ensuring alignment between business strategic ambitions and technology capabilities. You will contribute to a collaborative and innovative environment focused on people development.
 iA Financial Group is looking for an Enterprise Architect to join the Enterprise Architecture team. In your new role, you will play a strategic part in developing the organization’s evolution and modernization roadmaps, working closely with corporate functions, IT shared services and business teams.
 What you’ll accomplish with us 
 As an Enterprise Architect, you will be at the heart of our mission. Your main responsibilities will include:
 Translate the organization’s strategic ambitions into current and future IT capabilities;
 Promote the reuse of technology solutions and capabilities;
 Develop and maintain solution evolution roadmaps;
 Support Solution Architecture Advisors to ensure alignment of recommendations;
 Identify opportunities to improve enterprise architecture standards and practices and contribute to their evolution;
 Maintain architecture repositories and support their evolution;
 Contribute to cost-benefit analyses of solutions;
 Oversee the assessment of technical capabilities and advocate for architectural recommendations;
 Guide teams in applying the architecture process.
 What could accelerate your success in this role 
 We are looking for someone who:
 Is recognized for their natural influence and strategic vision;
 Stands out for their ability to develop innovative solutions;
 Has significant experience in enterprise architecture, with more than 15 years of experience;
 Has a strong command of architecture frameworks such as TOGAF and Zachman;
 Has experience with SDLC, DevOps, ITSM, Agile and LEAN approaches and practices;
 Demonstrates a strong ability to influence and effectively advocate for the organization’s architectural strategies and directions with a diverse audience;
 Has a strong focus on cloud computing and virtualization;
 Has excellent proficiency in French, both spoken and written;
 Has an intermediate level of proficiency in English, as the incumbent will be required to collaborate daily, both verbally and in writing, with English-speaking partners and business units.
 Why you’ll love working with us 
 A work environment where learning and development come together with a shared pursuit of excellence;
 Artificial intelligence is in everyone’s hands, helping you increase your personal effectiveness while supporting the organization’s growth;
 A healthy, safe, equitable and inclusive environment where everyone’s potential can thrive and develop;
 The opportunity to work in a hybrid environment supported by flexibility and access to inspiring and innovative workspaces.
 Competitive benefits 
 Flexible group insurance;
 Competitive pension plan;
 Employee share purchase plan;
 Vacation, wellness and personal development days;
 Telemedicine services;
 Employee and Family Assistance Program;
 Ergonomic office furniture program;
 Performance bonus;
 Discounts on iA products;
 And more!
 Apply now and take the lead in your career, where your talent truly matters! 
 Hesitant to apply? 
 At iA, we believe in potential and value diverse experiences. If this role inspires you, take the leap and apply. Your place may be with us, and we want to get to know you!
 Location(s) 
Quebec / 1080, Grande Allee West 
 Other Possible Location(s) 
Montreal / 1981 McGill College Avenue 
 Company 
 iA Financial Group
 Posting End Date 
2027-01-30 
 Company Overview 
 iA Financial Group* is the strength of a company with a human side, with its over 8,000 employees. Together, we have earned the trust of our more than four million clients and 25,000 advisors who have chosen us for their insurance, savings, and wealth management.
 With over $200 billion in assets and half a billion invested in technological innovation, we’re a key player in the financial services industry in Canada and the United States. The secret to our success? Investing in you, one person at a time. Because, for over 125 years, we have believed that it’s by supporting our employees and surrounding ourselves with the most reputable leaders in the industry, we will continue to innovate.
 At iA, we’re invested in you.
